The 0BSD grant above applies to cohost's OWN original source: the codemod
(src/cohost/rewrite.cljc), the shim (src/cohost/shim.cljc), the boot loop and
loader (src/cohost/boot.cljc), the policy, the host adapter contract and the
host adapters (src/cohost/adapter.cljc, src/cohost/hosts/**), the batteries,
the corpus scoreboard, the dev scripts (dev/**), the build files and the
documentation. cohost claims no copyright over any of it.

cohost does NOT relicense anyone else's code. It boots the real, unmodified
Clojure sources vendored under resources/cohost/clojure-1.12.0/: Clojure
1.12.0's clojure/core.clj, its companion files and the clojure.* libraries it
loads, from the clojure-1.12.0 release jar, and clojure.spec.alpha 0.5.238,
from its release jar. Those files are:

    Copyright (c) Rich Hickey. All rights reserved.
    (clojure/repl.clj: Copyright (c) Chris Houser, Dec 2008.
     All rights reserved.)
    Licensed under the Eclipse Public License 1.0 (EPL-1.0).

For that vendored code, the upstream copyright and license PASS THROUGH
UNCHANGED. cohost imposes nothing on it: the 0BSD grant above does not apply
to those files. They are byte for byte the files in the release jars, with
their copyright and license headers intact, and the EPL-1.0 text travels with
them (resources/cohost/clojure-1.12.0/LICENSE-EPL-v10.html). cohost's codemod
rewrites their forms only in memory, as they load; no file on disk is edited.
See NOTICE.md for full provenance.
